          "type": "open",
          "q": "Fill in the blanks: (i) If the mode of 12, 16, 19, 16, x, 12, 16, 19, 12 is 16, then x = ____. (ii) If the median of a data is 24 and each item is increased by 2, the new median is ____.",
          "answer": "(i) 12 occurs 3 times and 16 three times; for 16 to be the only mode it must occur more, so x = 16.\n(ii) Adding 2 to every item adds 2 to the median: 26.",
          "years": [
            "October 2024"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "2.2",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Write True or False: (i) Class mark is a measure of central tendency. (ii) The median of 3, 1, 5, 2, 4 is 5.",
          "answer": "(i) False: mean, median and mode are; a class mark is just a class's midpoint.\n(ii) False: in order 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 the middle value is 3."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.3",
          "type": "open",
          "q": "Fill in the blanks: (i) Two measures of central tendency are ____ and ____. (ii) The mean of 9 observations is 35; if 81 was misread as 18, the correct mean is ____.",
